# Task
Predict the action the target player is most likely to perform, not the theoretically optimal action.
Analyze the full observed rally and all retrieved cases. Treat the cases as behavioral evidence rather than action templates. Weight each case by its relevance to the current decision, especially:
- incoming shot and landing position;
- player and opponent positions;
- previous and required movement;
- rally sequence and phase;
- match score and context;
- time pressure and physical difficulty;
- player-specific style or condition.
Prioritize cases matching the most decision-relevant conditions and downweight superficial similarities. Infer the player's behavioral tendencies and adapt them to the current situation; the prediction may differ from every retrieved case.

